Subject: [PATCH 2/5] robo(slabs): show Batch Number / Design / Target Slabs
 inline in slab Edit
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The batch-split fields were built as a separate "split a mixed run" block; this
moves them inline alongside Production Date and Thickness so the Edit form reads
as one consistent set of fields, each with the same "Apply to this slab and every
following one in the batch, up to the next change." checkbox.

Behaviour is unchanged: Batch Number and Design live on the batch, so ticking
apply-forward re-parents this slab and the ones after it (up to the next batch
change) into that batch — how two runs recorded as one (1372/1404, 1384/1385)
get separated. Same server range mechanism (forwardRunIds / batchSplit.ts). No
schema change.

