Reference Sheet fixes:
- Robot Delays were matched by the stored delayCode.category ("ROBOT"), which is
  blank/inconsistent on old rows, so the row came out empty. Now matched by the
  CODE (C1…C20, the "G — Robot Delays" section) via isRobotDelayCode — robust to
  the category. Grouped by code: one row per code with its durations SUMMED (a
  code that hit 7 slabs is one row, not seven) and the Robos responsible unioned
  across all its entries (machineName can be several Robos), ordered C1…C20.
  e.g. "C1 — Frame Cleaning (Robo1, Robo4) → 37 minutes".
- Robo Program Names and Robot Delays now print ONE ROW PER program / per code,
  not joined into a single cell.
- Removed the explanatory "Note" row from the sheet, and the descriptive blurb
  from the Downloads section on the website — kept clean and data-only.
- Design search is already case-insensitive (designMatchKey lower-cases both
  sides); added a test pinning it. All figures still come from the DB; nothing
  hardcoded. No schema change.

